But that's not all. I've also got a half-formed idea regarding the
'immune to everything' problem, again regarding resistances. There are
a few aspects of this idea. The first point is that some intrinsics
are less powerful than their extrinsic counter-parts =96 telepathy and
speed for example. The same could be done with resistances. Resistance
from external sources, such as rings and armour, could work as it does
now: essentially 'immunity' rather than 'resistance'; and intrinsic
resistance could be made less powerful. The particular 'less powerful'
version I have in mind involves a kind of cooldown period between
attacks. So, for example if you were hitting a blue jelly and you have
intrinsic cold resistance, you might get no message for the first
attack, and then "You feel a mild chill", then "You feel quite cold",
then finally "You are suddenly very cold!" The resistance would return
again after some turns.

I haven't thought much about how this would be implemented, but I
imagine that behind-the-scenes it would be a kind of regenerating
damage shield.

Also, since many cold/fire/lightning attacks are ray based, I was
thinking that maybe reflection could be nerfed so that a new
resistance system like this would get more play. Reflection could have
a similar kind of cooldown like I described for resistance - blocking
the first ray 100% of the time, but then having the probability
reduced for awhile with each successive reflection. Or maybe not.

